description:
INPUT: src/things_mcp/main.py already has health-check helpers (perform_health_check, test_applescript_connectivity) — read and consolidate; do not duplicate.
OUTPUT: 'mcp-server-things doctor' (and 'python -m things_mcp doctor') printing a PASS/FAIL/WARN table with a one-line fix hint per row, exit non-zero on any FAIL:
[1] Things 3 installed (mdfind kMDItemCFBundleIdentifier=com.culturedcode.ThingsMac or /Applications path);
[2] Things 3 running (osascript 'application "Things3" is running');
[3] Automation permission (osascript 'tell application "Things3" to get name'; map error -1743 'not authorized to send Apple events' to: System Settings > Privacy & Security > Automation > enable Things 3 for the host app);
[4] Database readable via things.py (things.inbox() or things.today() with a short timeout; map sqlite 'unable to open database file' to the TCC fix hint: grant Full Disk Access to the launching binary, or run via HTTP transport from Terminal — link the TCC troubleshooting section);
[5] uv/uvx on PATH (WARN only; hint: brew install uv);
[6] auth token file present (.things-auth or ~/.things-auth; INFO only, needed for URL-scheme features);
[7] Python version + fastmcp version.
Also --json for machine output. Doctor must never modify Things data.
TESTS: unit tests with subprocess/things patched covering each check's PASS and FAIL mapping (esp. -1743 and 'unable to open database file').
DONE: doctor runs end-to-end on this Mac (manual; report output); tests pass; README Troubleshooting points to it first; CHANGELOG.
